UPDATE companies SET description='LMC Industries operates from Arnold, Missouri, where it was founded in 1945 by toolmaker Fred Suellentrop Sr. The company remains family-owned and traces its start to Suellentrop''s goal of building high-quality equipment that improves the manufacturability of essential products.

The company provides precision metal stamping — including progressive die stamping, in-die tapping, and in-die assembly — alongside plastic injection molding, insert molding, and overmolding. It also runs a 14,000-square-foot tool room equipped with CNC milling, wire and conventional EDM, water jet machining, and TIG welding for in-house die and mold fabrication, repair, and maintenance. All operations share a 240,000-square-foot facility housing more than 80 stamping and injection molding presses.

LMC serves OEMs and tiered suppliers in automotive, agricultural, consumer products, medical device, and hand-tool markets. Automotive customers include every major global automaker; agricultural programs cover harvesting equipment and livestock feeding systems; consumer products range from screwdriver and toothbrush handles to medical device grips and automotive interior touchpoints.

The company emphasizes a single-source model for metal and plastic components, which it says simplifies purchasing, compresses lead times, and creates a single point of quality accountability. Its differentiators include Design for Manufacturability applied to every program, a transfer-tooling process for taking over existing programs, PPAP and APQP quality systems with first-article inspection, and a dedicated team focused on proactive communication.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision metal stamping", "Progressive die stamping", "In-die tapping", "In-die assembly", "Plastic injection molding", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Tool and die fabrication", "Tool and die maintenance", "Assembly and finishing", "Welding", "Riveting", "Chemical passivation", "Logistics and kitting", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM)", "Advanced Product Quality Planning (APQP)", "Production Part Approval Process (PPAP)", "First article inspection"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Agricultural", "Consumer products", "Medical devices", "Hand tools"], "materials": ["Metals", "Engineered plastics"], "equipment": ["CNC milling", "Wire EDM", "Conventional EDM", "Water jet machining", "TIG welding", "Metal stamping presses", "Plastic injection molding presses"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source production of both metal stampings and plastic molded parts in one facility", "In-house 14,000 sq ft tool room with CNC milling, wire EDM, conventional EDM, water jet machining, and TIG welding", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM) applied to every program across metal and plastic processes", "Transfer tooling process to onboard existing programs from other suppliers with minimal disruption", "PPAP and APQP quality systems with first-article inspections and ongoing tooling maintenance"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1945 by Fred Suellentrop Sr. -> /about-us", "Family-owned -> /about-us", "Headquarters Arnold, Missouri -> db", "240,000+ sq ft facility -> /, /capabilities", "80+ stamping and injection molding presses -> /", "20 stamping presses in 86,000 sq ft -> /", "14,000 sq ft tool room with CNC milling, wire EDM, conventional EDM, water jet machining, TIG welding -> /, /capabilities", "In-house die and mold fabrication, repair, maintenance -> /capabilities", "Capabilities: precision metal stamping, progressive die stamping, in-die tapping, in-die assembly, plastic injection molding, insert molding, overmolding, tool & die, assembly & finishing, logistics -> /capabilities", "Assembly services: welding, riveting, chemical passivation -> /", "Quality: PPAP, APQP, first article inspections -> /, /quality", "Industries: automotive (every major worldwide), agricultural (harvesting equipment, livestock feeding), consumer products (screwdriver handles, toothbrush handles, medical device grips, automotive interior touchpoints), hand tools -> /, db", "Single-source metal and plastic under one roof -> /capabilities", "DFM applied to every program -> /capabilities", "Transfer tooling process -> /capabilities", "Certifications: ISO9001, IATF16949 -> db", "Materials: metals, engineered plastics -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We design and fabricate metal stamping parts and plastic injection molded parts either as standalone products or combined as insert-molded or over-molded assemblies.", "founded_year": "1945", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lmc-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Locust Grove Woodworks operates from Thorndike, Maine, where it was founded in 1982 by a craftsman who spent much of his life in Amish and Mennonite communities. The founder''s background in those ascetical traditions shaped a philosophy of simplicity, durability, and sustainable production that still guides the shop today.

The one-person workshop produces heirloom-grade solid-wood furniture piece by piece, using a mix of hand tools and power equipment driven partly by draft horses. Construction relies on traditional joinery such as sliding dovetails and floating tenons to accommodate wood movement, and finishes are hand-applied linseed oil and wax. The catalog spans beds, chairs, tables, desks, clocks, cradles, coffins, and custom casework.

Each item is built to order, with no inventory of mass-produced stock.

The business was started to create furniture that could be passed down for generations, inspired by the Shaker maxim to build as if you were to live a thousand years but die tomorrow. The founder''s commitment to low-impact, horse-powered manufacturing remains a defining characteristic.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Handcrafted solid wood furniture", "Custom furniture design and build", "Casework", "Traditional joinery (sliding dovetails, floating tenons)", "Hand-applied linseed oil and wax finishing", "Horse-powered machining operations"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Custom woodworking"], "materials": ["Solid wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Each piece built one at a time by a single craftsman", "Workshop powered partly by draft horses and lineshafts", "Solid-wood construction with traditional joinery (sliding dovetails, floating tenons)", "Hand-applied linseed oil and wax finishes", "Heirloom quality designed for generational use"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 -> db", "Headquarters Thorndike, Maine -> db", "Founder''s Amish/Mennonite background -> /", "Shaker design influence -> /", "Horse-powered workshop -> /", "Handcrafted solid wood furniture with traditional joinery -> /", "Sole proprietor working alone -> /", "Product categories: beds, chairs, clocks, coffins, cradles, desks, tables -> /", "Linseed oil and wax finishes -> /", "Address 256 Ward Hill Road, Thorndike, Maine 04986 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "I have been building fine quality furniture and wood products since 1982.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "1", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='locust-grove-woodworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Lodge Factory Store opened in 1994 in South Pittsburg, Tennessee, as an outlet for factory-second cast iron pieces that fell short of the company''s quality standards.

Over time the location grew from a seconds shop into a full-line retailer carrying the entire Lodge catalog: classic skillets, Dutch ovens, griddles, grill pans, the Fluted Cake Pan and Wedge Pan, enameled cast iron Dutch ovens, professional-grade carbon steel cookware, stoneware baking dishes, and a wide range of accessories.

