UPDATE companies SET description='Louisiana Tech University is a public university located in Ruston, Louisiana. Founded on July 6, 1894, as a selective-admissions comprehensive institution, it has grown into a campus centered around a pedestrian-friendly quad in a town of approximately 22,000 residents.

Total enrollment stands at 12,039 students with a student-faculty ratio of 21:1. The academic calendar operates on a quarter system that awards semester hours, and over 90% of students receive some form of financial assistance.

Louisiana Tech serves students pursuing fields such as engineering (biomedical, chemical, civil, computer, cyber, electrical, industrial, mechanical), business (accounting, finance, management, marketing), health sciences (nursing, medical laboratory science, health informatics), computer science, education, liberal arts, and applied sciences. The institution also engages in workforce development and research partnerships, though specific industry clients are not detailed in the source material.

The university emphasizes hands-on learning and real-world applications, particularly in engineering. It is ranked the #1 Public University in Louisiana by Niche (2026), placed in the top 7% of universities worldwide by the Center for World Universities Rankings (2024), and recognized for the #1 highest early career earnings in Louisiana. The Bulldogs compete in 16 varsity sports at the NCAA Division I level in the Sun Belt Conference.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": [], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hands-on learning approach with real-world applications", "Selective admissions and comprehensive public university mission", "Quarter-based academic calendar awarding semester hours", "Over 90% of students receive financial assistance", "NCAA Division I athletics in the Sun Belt Conference"], "facts_used": ["Founded July 6, 1894 in Ruston, Louisiana -> /about", "Public university, selective-admissions, comprehensive -> /about", "Total enrollment 12,039, student-faculty ratio 21:1 -> /about", "Quarter system awarding semester hours -> /about", "Over 90% students receive financial assistance -> /about", "16 varsity sports, NCAA Division I Sun Belt Conference -> /about", "#1 Public University in Louisiana (Niche, 2026) -> /", "Top 7% of universities worldwide (CWUR, 2024) -> /", "14th straight year Top Tier National University (U.S. News, 2025) -> /", "#1 Highest Early Career Earnings in Louisiana -> /", "135 degrees & programs -> /", "Campus centered around Quad, Ruston population ~22,000 -> /about"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Louisiana Tech University, established in 1894 in Ruston, Louisiana, is renowned for its commitment to academic excellence and hands-on learning.", "founded_year": "1894", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='louisiana-tech-university' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Loving West Virginia operates from Fairmont, West Virginia, selling state-themed merchandise through its e-commerce site lovingwv.com. The founding year and ownership structure are not disclosed in the available sources.

The company offers a range of West Virginia–branded consumer products including Cryptid Playing Cards featuring Mothman, Bigfoot, Flatwoods Monster, and Batboy; apparel collections for adults and youth; vinyl decals; 8×10 art prints on 100 lb cardstock; glassware; can coolers; a 55-county scratch-off map; and a monthly mystery-sticker subscription club. Flood-relief fundraiser shirts and stickers are also part of the lineup.

