UPDATE companies SET description='MADE Apparel Services was founded in 2020 in Renton, Washington, by Heather Zager. The firm operates as an independent product development studio.

The company provides end-to-end product development for sewn goods, including pattern making using CLO3D and Alvanon digital forms, sewn prototyping, pattern grading with industry-standard CAD tools, and tech pack creation. They also offer apparel consulting and concept development. The team consists of Zager and administrative support Nirosha Rodrigo, working with clients from initial concept through production-ready deliverables.

MADE serves startups, established brands, and corporate teams developing apparel and sewn products. Client projects span equestrian apparel (Whinny Equestrian), postpartum recovery garments (Luna Azzurra Care), sustainable womenswear (Springtime & Harvest), activewear for large-chested women (Wrax), and functional accessories (The Book Carrier Bookmark).

Zager started the business to bring structured, transparent development to creators who lack technical design resources, emphasizing that better products come from better information. The consultancy differentiates itself by using 3D simulation to evaluate fit and construction early, reducing revisions and waste before manufacturing begins.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pattern making", "Pattern development", "Sewn prototyping", "Pattern grading", "Tech pack creation", "Apparel consulting", "Concept development", "3D garment simulation", "Digital pattern making", "Fit evaluation", "Sample review and revision management"], "industries": ["Equestrian apparel", "Postpartum recovery garments", "Sustainable womenswear", "Activewear", "Functional accessories"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CLO3D", "Alvanon digital forms", "Industry-standard CAD tools"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Structured, transparent development process", "3D garment simulation with CLO3D and Alvanon digital forms", "Production-ready deliverables including graded patterns and tech packs", "Free Founder''s Guide to the Stages of Product Development", "Founder teaches patternmaking at Seattle Central College"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2020 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Renton, Washington -> db, /", "Founder Heather Zager -> /about", "Administrative support Nirosha Rodrigo -> /about", "Services: pattern making, sewn samples, pattern grading, tech packs, apparel consulting -> /, /services", "Tools: CLO3D, Alvanon digital forms, CAD -> /, /services", "Client examples: Whinny Equestrian, Luna Azzurra Care, Springtime & Harvest, Wrax, The Book Carrier Bookmark -> /", "Company description: sewn product development consultancy -> /", "Founder background: Seattle Central College, Meta, teaching -> /about", "Mission: structured transparent approach, better products from better information -> /about"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_product