UPDATE companies SET description='MAGNA Pharmaceuticals, Inc. was founded on August 1, 1990, in Louisville, Kentucky, as a family-owned pharmaceutical company. The business remains under family ownership and is led by President and CEO Dr. Warren P. Lesser, who emphasizes accountability as a core value.

The company develops and manufactures a range of pharmaceutical products and dietary supplements, including the antihistamine Stahist T (triprolidine) in scored tablets that allow half-tablet dosing.

MAGNA serves the pharmaceutical, specialty pharma, and healthcare sectors, with particular focus on wound care, ostomy, and continence markets. It holds memberships in the Wound, Ostomy, and Continence Nurses Society and the Specialty Pharma Association, reflecting its engagement with clinical professionals and specialty distributors.

The company’s stated mission is to provide non‑substitutable products and services at reasonable prices with genuine concern for stakeholders. Dr. Lesser has said, “We really want to help people. If all we do is make money, we haven’t done anything with our lives that has real value,” underscoring a patient‑focused philosophy.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pharmaceutical manufacturing", "Dietary supplement manufacturing", "Tablet scoring and custom dosing", "Product formulation"], "industries": ["Pharmaceuticals", "Dietary supplements", "Wound care", "Ostomy care", "Continence care", "Specialty pharmaceuticals"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned with accountability-focused culture", "Non\u2011substitutable pharmaceutical products at reasonable prices", "Scored tablets enabling customized half\u2011tablet dosing", "Membership in WOCN Society and Specialty Pharma Association", "High-standard manufacturing of pharmaceuticals and supplements"], "facts_used": ["Founded August 1, 1990 -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Louisville, KY -> /about-us, db", "Family-owned business -> /about-us", "President & CEO Dr. Warren P. Lesser -> /about-us", "Manufactures pharmaceutical products and supplements -> /about-us", "Stahist T (triprolidine) scored tablets -> db", "Member of Wound, Ostomy, and Continence Nurses Society -> /about-us", "Member of Specialty Pharma Association -> /about-us", "Mission: non-substitutable products at reasonable prices -> /about-us", "Accountability tagline -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "MAGNA Pharmaceuticals was founded on August 1, 1990 and is a United States pharmaceutical company owned and operated in Louisville, KY. We specialize in unique high-quality pharmaceutical products and supplements", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='magna-pharmaceuticals-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='MCT Industries Inc. was founded in 1974 as a family-owned operation in Albuquerque, New Mexico. The company began with trailer sales and repairs and has since expanded into a full-service provider for truck bodies, trailers, and heavy equipment.

Today MCT operates a custom fabrication facility equipped with a plasma cutter, laser cutter, 20-foot press brake, and shear. The shop installs and customizes flatbeds, service bodies, dump bodies, crane bodies, and hydraulic systems, while also performing DOT inspections and building custom trailers. A parts department stocks more than 10,000 components covering over 200 equipment and trailer types, supporting both light- and heavy-duty applications.

The customer base spans government and commercial sectors. MCT holds state and CES contracts and serves state, city, and county entities across New Mexico, as well as military and federal agencies through a dedicated government manufacturing plant that handles design through full-rate production. The waste division provides roll-off service in Albuquerque and residential collection in Santa Fe, while the commercial division supplies parts, sales, service, and rentals for trailers and heavy equipment used in construction, snow removal, and agricultural spraying.

The company emphasizes its four-decade track record and a parts team experienced in locating hard-to-find components. Its government manufacturing plant offers end-to-end production from prototype to full-rate runs, a capability the firm highlights as a key differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom fabrication", "Plasma cutting", "Laser cutting", "Press brake forming", "Shearing", "Hydraulic systems service", "Refuse vehicle service", "Dump body installation", "Flatbed installation", "Crane body installation", "Service body installation", "DOT inspections", "Salt spreader installation", "Snow plow installation", "Wetline kit installation", "Combo kit installation", "Walking floor installation", "End dump installation", "Spray kit installation", "Trailer sales", "Equipment rentals", "Roll-off service", "Parts sales"], "industries": ["State government", "Municipal government", "Military", "Waste management", "Commercial fleet", "Construction", "Snow removal", "Agriculture"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Plasma Cutter", "Laser Cutter", "20'' Press Brake", "Shear"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Stocks over 10,000 parts for 200+ equipment types", "40+ years in business", "Family-owned and operated", "Holds state and CES contracts", "Government manufacturing plant with design-to-production capability"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1974 -> /about", "Family-owned and operated -> /about", "Headquarters Albuquerque, New Mexico -> db", "Stocks over 10,000 parts for 200+ equipment types -> /", "Equipment: Plasma Cutter, Laser Cutter, 20'' Press Brake, Shear -> /", "State and CES contracts -> /", "Government manufacturing plant design to full-rate production -> /about", "Waste division roll-off service Albuquerque, residential Santa Fe -> /about", "Custom fabrication capabilities (flatbeds, service bodies, dump bodies, crane bodies) -> /", "Trailer sales (light and heavy duty) -> /", "DOT inspections -> /", "Snow plow and salt spreader installation -> /", "Wetline kits, combo kits, walking floors, end dumps, spray kits -> /", "Hydraulic systems service -> /", "Refuse vehicle service -> /", "Equipment rentals -> /", "Parts sales -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "MCT''s Government manufacturing plant works with our customers from design and prototype development to full rate production", "founded_year": "1974", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mct-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='MEI Electrical Contractors & Systems Integrators is headquartered in Westfield, Vermont. The business traces its roots to 1991 when it was founded as Mike’s Electric, Inc. in Jay, Vermont. A branch office opened in Williston in 2013 to serve Chittenden County and western Vermont. In 2017, then‑President Adam Fortier purchased the company and relocated it to a larger facility in Westfield.

The firm operates as a full‑service electrical contractor and systems integrator. Its scope covers electrical design, installation, maintenance, testing, inspection, repair, and monitoring, along with fire alarm and security system design, installation, and monitoring. Additional services include design/build project delivery, lighting design and energy conservation, electrical service upgrades, 24‑hour emergency response, network infrastructure, access control, video surveillance, fiber optic installation, and solar/renewable energy projects. The workforce numbers over 65, including Master and Journeymen electricians, and the company participates in the Vermont Registered Apprenticeship program to train new electrical workers.

MEI serves commercial, industrial, health care, educational, agricultural, governmental (federal, state, and local), and residential customers throughout Vermont, New Hampshire, New York, Maine, and Massachusetts. It maintains long‑standing relationships with general contractors such as DEW Construction Corp., PeakCM, Bread Loaf Corporation, ReArch Company, Wright & Morrissey, and Kingsbury Companies, and holds multi‑year state and federal contracts for electrical, fire alarm, and security work.

The company states its mission is to deliver efficient, quality work at competitive prices, completing projects on time and on budget using current technology and a highly skilled workforce. It emphasizes a family‑focused workplace, a strong safety record, and ongoing employee education and advancement opportunities as foundations for sustained growth.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical design and installation", "Electrical maintenance, testing, inspection, repair", "Fire alarm system design, installation, monitoring", "Security system design, installation, monitoring", "Network infrastructure installation", "Access control systems", "Video surveillance systems", "Fiber optic installation", "Design/build project delivery", "Lighting design and energy conservation", "Electrical service upgrades", "24-hour emergency electrical service", "Solar and renewable energy system installation"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Industrial", "Health care", "Educational", "Agricultural", "Governmental", "Residential"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["25-year track record in electrical, fire alarm, and security systems", "Over 65 employees including Master and Journeymen electricians", "Vermont Registered Apprenticeship program for workforce development", "24-hour emergency service availability", "Multi-year state and federal government contracts across five states"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters Westfield, Vermont -> db", "Founded 1991 as Mike''s Electric, Inc. -> /about", "Adam Fortier purchased business in 2017 -> /about", "Branch office Williston opened 2013 -> /about", "Over 65 employees including Master/Journeymen electricians -> /about", "Vermont Registered Apprenticeship program participation -> /about", "Services: electrical, fire alarm, security, network, access control, video surveillance, fiber optics, design/build, lighting, service upgrades, 24-hour emergency, solar -