UPDATE companies SET description='MRL Equipment Company operates from Billings, Montana, where it has built pavement marking, removal, grooving, and pavement maintenance equipment for more than three decades. The business was started by road stripers who brought first-hand experience from striping and removal operations, shaping a company that designs machinery around the practical needs of the people who use it daily.

The company produces a range of specialized trucks and systems, including thermoplastic applicators with 12,000‑lb and 16,000‑lb capacity, the EpoxyPro plural‑component impingement mixing system, removal and grooving trucks that use a multiple‑head progressive removal system to limit surface damage, and road marking and raised‑pavement‑marker equipment designed for high‑volume output and ease of service. MRL also offers retrofit kits, parts support, and financing options to keep fleets running.

The company’s "built by stripers, for stripers" philosophy means each machine is developed with direct input from the operators who will run it.

