' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Majestic Metals by Fathom Manufacturing operates a sheet metal fabrication facility in Denver, Colorado. The business was founded in 1979 as Majestic Metals and has accumulated more than 45 years of experience in precision fabrication. Today it operates as part of the Fathom Manufacturing network, maintaining the same end-to-end approach that defined its early years.

The Denver facility takes parts from cutting and forming through finishing and final assembly, delivering complete fabricated products rather than loose components. Core processes include laser cutting (fiber, solid-state, and CO2), CNC punching, press-brake forming up to 12 feet and 220 tons, welding (arc, MIG, TIG, spot, and laser), captive hardware installation, painting, powder coating, screen printing, mechanical and electro-mechanical assembly, and in-house CNC machining for post-mill features. The shop runs three fiber/solid-state lasers, two CO2 lasers, five punch presses, thirteen press brakes, twelve TIG welders, seven MIG welders, and one laser welder, with automated loading that enables lights-out production for runs of 100 to 10,000 pieces. Work spans prototype through full production across aluminum, steel, and stainless steel from 0.010 to 0.50 inch thick, holding ±0.005 inch on cutting and punching.

The facility serves data-center and IT infrastructure, EV charging equipment, medical device housings, self-service kiosks and retail technology, industrial equipment enclosures, military and defense, automotive, energy, agriculture, semiconductor, and consumer electronics and lighting. Customers include a major semiconductor manufacturer that cites accuracy, flatness, and consistency across runs.

The company emphasizes a single-source model that eliminates multi-vendor coordination, a value-engineering mindset applied from prototype to production, design-for-manufacturability support, and a 98% on-time delivery rate. ITAR registration allows it to handle government and defense projects.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision sheet metal fabrication", "Laser cutting (fiber, solid-state, CO2)", "CNC punching", "Press brake forming and bending", "Welding (arc, MIG, TIG, spot, laser)", "Captive hardware installation", "Painting", "Powder coating", "Screen printing", "Mechanical assembly", "Kitting", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "CNC machining", "Soft tool manufacturing", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Value engineering", "Lights-out production", "Laser inspection", "Prototyping", "Production runs"], "industries": ["Data centers and IT infrastructure", "EV charging equipment", "Medical device housings", "Self-service kiosks and retail technology", "Industrial equipment enclosures", "Military and defense", "Automotive", "Energy", "Agriculture", "Semiconductor", "Consumer electronics and lighting"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Steel", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": ["Three fiber and solid-state lasers", "Two CO2 lasers", "Five punch presses", "Thirteen press brakes (up to 12 ft, 220 tons)", "Twelve TIG welders", "Seven MIG welders", "One laser welder", "Automated loading/unloading equipment"], "volume": "Prototype to production; lights-out production 100 to 10,000 units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.005 in for laser cutting and CNC punching; tighter tolerances possible", "built_on": ["Complete fabricated products under one roof: cutting, forming, finishing, graphics, and assembly", "Single-source model that removes multi-vendor management", "Lights-out production for volumes of 100 to 10,000 pieces", "In-house CNC machining for post-mill features without delaying turnaround", "ITAR registered 