UPDATE companies SET description='Maple Lane Farms operates from Charleston, Maine, on a property first purchased by Stanley Higgins in 1935. The farm passed to Charles “Shine” and Margaret Higgins in 1941 and evolved from a potato, dairy, and hay operation into a multi-generation family business. In 1999, Barry and Mary Higgins acquired the farm from Charles and established the current Maple Lane Farms entity, continuing a lineage that now spans five generations.

The farm raises approximately 700 head of cattle and processes its own beef, pork, and chicken in a state-inspected facility expanded in 2005 and again in 2011 to add refrigeration and an automated smokehouse. Operations include custom slaughter and cutting for outside livestock, hay and silage production (round and square bales stored indoors), and screened compost made from processing waste, cow manure, and horse barn waste. A retail store sells flash-frozen cuts, sausages, bacon, and the farm’s “Black Label Reserve” beef, with orders filled Monday through Friday.

Customers include local households buying retail meat, farmers needing custom processing for their own animals, horse owners purchasing horse-quality hay, and gardeners using the farm’s compost. The farm also supplies feed and serves as one of the largest hay dealers in the Northeast, selling silage by the ton and hay by the bale.

The Higgins family emphasizes hands-on work—every cut, sausage link, and label is done by hand—and the farm’s diversification was driven by the need to sustain the operation through changing regulations and market pressures.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom meat processing (state-inspected)", "Retail meat cutting and packaging", "Flash freezing", "Sausage making", "Bacon curing", "Hay baling (round and square)", "Silage production", "Compost screening and production", "Feed sales", "Black Label Reserve beef program"], "industries": ["Hay dealers", "Meat processing", "Composting", "Feed sales", "Retail meat sales"], "materials": ["Beef", "Pork", "Chicken", "Hay", "Silage", "Compost (processing waste, cow manure, horse manure)"], "equipment": ["Automated smoke house", "Refrigeration equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Orders filled Monday-Friday; weekend orders processed following Monday", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hand-processed products (every cut, sausage, label done by hand)", "Flash-frozen immediately after processing, no old stock", "State-inspected processing facility with automated smokehouse", "One of the largest hay dealers in the Northeast"], "facts_used": ["Location: Charleston, Maine -> db", "Founding: Stanley Higgins bought farm in 1935 -> /about", "Ownership: Family-owned, five generations -> /about, /", "Facility: State-inspected processing facility expanded 2005, automated smokehouse added 2011 -> /about", "Herd size: ~700 cows -> /about", "Products: Beef, pork, chicken, hay, silage, compost -> /, /about", "Custom processing for customer livestock -> /, /about", "Retail store with flash-frozen cuts, sausages, bacon, Black Label Reserve -> /", "Hay: round and square bales, horse quality, stored indoors, net wrapped -> /about", "Compost: screened, made from processing waste, cow waste, horse barn waste -> /about", "Feed sales -> /", "Order fulfillment: Monday-Friday, weekend orders next Monday -> /", "Hand-processed emphasis -> /", "Largest hay dealers in Northeast -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom processing in a state inspected facility for customers who raise their own animals. We also process our own animals into cuts for the retail store, as well as for customers who wish to order whole, sides, hind or fore quarter beef from us.", "founded_year": "1935", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='maple-lane-farms-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mar-Med was founded in 1989 in Grand Rapids, Michigan, by Dr. Joseph Marogil, a general surgeon who invented the Tourni-Cot digital tourniquet to address a need he encountered in hand surgery. The company remains physician-founded and family-owned, operating from its original location near the city’s Medical Mile.

Today Mar-Med operates as an FDA-registered medical device manufacturing site certified to ISO 13485:2016. It designs and produces a line of disposable devices including the Tourni-Cot and Uni-Cot digit tourniquets, the Rhino-Pak epistaxis balloon, the Balloon Extractor for nasal foreign-body removal, the Derma-Stent abscess drain, and the ZEROWET wound-irrigation system. The company also handles global distribution of these products to healthcare facilities worldwide.

Mar-Med’s devices are used in emergency medicine, podiatry, pediatrics, and orthopedic surgery, serving hospitals, clinics, and other healthcare providers across the United States and internationally. The company emphasizes simple, cost-effective tools that support efficient procedures and positive patient outcomes.

The firm cites its family-owned structure, physician-led design perspective, and compliance with FDA QSR, ISO 13485, and European CE marking requirements as key differentiators. It also highlights sustainability practices such as composting label backing, recycling eligible waste, and reusing packaging materials.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','FDA QSR (21 CFR Part 820)','CE Mark (Directive 93/42/EEC)','CE Mark (MDR EU 2017/745)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical device manufacturing", "Product design and development", "Global distribution", "FDA QSR compliance", "ISO 13485 quality management", "CE marking compliance"], "industries": ["Emergency medicine", "Podiatry", "Pediatrics", "Orthopedic surgery", "Healthcare facilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["FDA-registered manufacturing site with ISO 13485:2016 certification", "Family-owned and physician-founded since 1989", "CE-marked products for European market access", "Sustainability program including composting, recycling, and packaging reuse", "Global distribution network for disposable medical devices"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989 by Dr. Joseph Marogil in Grand Rapids, Michigan -> /about-us", "Physician-founded, family-owned -> /about-us, /", "FDA registered manufacturing site certified to ISO 13485:2016 -> /about-us, /quality", "Products: Tourni-Cot, Uni-Cot, Rhino-Pak, Balloon Extractor, Derma-Stent, ZEROWET -> /", "Industries served: emergency medicine, podiatry, pediatrics, orthopedic surgery -> /about-us", "CE marking for EU market (Directive 93/42/EEC, MDR EU 2017/745) -> /quality", "Sustainability practices: composting, recycling, reuse -> /about-us", "Headquarters: Grand Rapids, Michigan -> /about-us, /", "LinkedIn URL -> db", "Founded year 1989 -> db", "ISO 13485 certification -> db, /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Mar-Med is an FDA registered American medical device manufacturing site certified to ISO 13485:2016", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/mar-med-co./"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mar-med' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Marelli North America, Inc. is headquartered in Lewisburg, Tennessee. The company''s motorsport division traces its origins to 1919, when Marelli began developing electronic and electro-mechanical systems for two- and four-wheel racing vehicles.

The company designs and manufactures automotive lighting, electronics, interiors, propulsion, exhaust, chassis, and thermal systems. It also provides hardware development platforms for software-defined vehicles and offers telemetry, hybrid and electric powertrain systems, and fuel components for motorsport applications. Marelli operates 32 sites globally certified under SA8000 and reports that 88% of its electricity comes from renewable sources.

Marelli serves automakers and racing teams across Formula 1, MotoGP, and the World Endurance Championship. Its customer base includes carmakers seeking co-creation partnerships for vehicle personalization, sustainable energy management, and software-defined vehicle architectures.

