UPDATE companies SET description='Marsh Electronics, Inc. traces its roots to 1935 when Earl Marsh and Kathleen Meek founded Marsh Radio Supply Co. in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. The company rebranded as Marsh Electronics in 1973 and has operated independently since 1998 after a series of acquisitions and a management buyback. Today it is headquartered in Milwaukee, serving the North Central United States from its base there.

The firm operates as a broad-line distributor of electronic and electromechanical components, augmented by a value-added division called MarVac Assemblies. Marsh also offers inventory replenishment programs, vendor reduction solutions, and engineering support with an on-staff engineer who assists with component selection, application research, and custom circuit design. The company''s facility includes automated equipment such as a Komax wire cutting machine and the MKE1 system installed in 2022.

Marsh serves original equipment manufacturers in commercial and off-road vehicles, energy (including solar heliostat tracking and energy storage), food and beverage processing, industrial equipment, medical devices, and military programs. Its supplier line card includes brands such as Eaton, Molex, Littelfuse, Sanyo Denki, and Carling Switch.

The company emphasizes its 90-year track record, ISO 9001:2015 certification, and a customer-relationship model focused on second- and third-tier accounts. It positions its engineering team and custom assembly capabilities as a way to streamline customers'' production and logistics processes.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assembly", "Wire harness assembly", "Wire processing (cutting, stripping, termination)", "Box build assembly", "Component application engineering support", "Inventory replenishment program", "Vendor reduction solutions", "Electronic component distribution", "Custom circuit design assistance", "Prototyping and sample provision"], "industries": ["Commercial & off-road vehicles", "Energy", "Food and beverage", "Industrial", "Medical", "Military"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Komax wire cutting machine", "MKE1 system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1935 as Marsh Radio Supply Co. by Earl Marsh and Kathleen Meek -> /about", "Headquartered in Milwaukee, Wisconsin -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "Custom assembly, wire processing, and cable capabilities -> /", "MarVac Assemblies division for value-added assembly -> /about", "Industries served: Commercial & Off-Road Vehicles, Energy, Food and Beverage, Industrial, Medical, Military -> /", "Komax wire cutting machine installed 2010 -> /about", "MKE1 system installed 2022 -> /about", "20,000 sq. ft. facility noted in 1975 -> /about", "Acquisition history and return to independence in 1998 -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Distributor of Electronic Components and Provider of Value Added Services", "founded_year": "1935", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='marsh-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Marsh Medical operates from Newell, West Virginia, as a dedicated medical component brand under Marsh Bellofram, a U.S. manufacturer with a history reaching back more than 125 years. The company emerged to consolidate nearly a half-century of experience designing and manufacturing critical medical device components into a single access point.

The company produces pressure and flow regulators, electro-pneumatic pressure and flow controls, transducers, electronic timing controls, open medical power supplies, and custom-engineered solutions. In-house engineers and chemists develop custom solutions, and the facility runs multiple production shifts — adding a second shift and six-day weeks during the COVID-19 pandemic to meet ventilator demand. The portfolio encompasses more than 100,000 custom part numbers ranging from precision air regulators and diaphragms to silicone components, electrical wiring, and thermocouples.

Marsh Medical serves the medical device industry, supplying components for ventilators and other critical medical equipment.

