UPDATE companies SET description='MediVena is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia, with additional offices in Poland. The company develops and markets medical devices for blood collection, diagnostics, injection systems, and personal protective equipment under the ONE-CARE® brand. While its founding year is not publicly disclosed, MediVena has established a presence across the Americas and Europe, serving healthcare providers through distribution partners.

The company’s product portfolio includes safety lancets, blood collection needles and winged sets, tube holders, safety pen needles, insulin syringes, glucose monitors, and alcohol prep pads. MediVena manages an end-to-end process from product design ideation and voice-of-customer research through fast prototyping, design verification, clinical trials, and regulatory approvals to commercialization. It operates a warehouse in Atlanta that ships orders within 48 hours with free ground shipping, and leverages a manufacturing base spanning the United States, Europe, Latin America, and Asia.

MediVena serves acute care hospitals, long-term care facilities, physician offices, blood banks, home health agencies, and the animal health market. Its customers include primary care practices, reference laboratories, and home care providers in both U.S. and international markets.

The company states its mission is to deliver innovative medical devices that are effective, affordable, entirely safe, and comfortable for patients and healthcare professionals. A recent grant-funded project (2021–2023) focused on developing a universal safety needle with minimized dead space and a fully automated manufacturing line, underscoring its focus on safety and process innovation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product design ideation", "Voice of customer and market research", "Modeling and fast prototyping", "Design verification and validation", "Clinical trials", "Implementation to production and regulatory approvals", "Commercialization", "Corporate go-to-market strategy", "Identification of potential business partners", "Contract negotiations", "Support in operations and registrations/regulatory activities", "Tactical sales and marketing", "Supply chain and inventory management", "Manufacturing and supplies"], "industries": ["AcuteCare", "Long Term Care", "Physician Offices", "Blood Banks", "Home Health", "Animal Health"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "48 hours for stocked items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Ships orders within 48 hours from Atlanta warehouse", "Free ground shipping to distribution partners", "End-to-end product development from ideation to commercialization", "Manufacturing footprint across US, Europe, Latin America, and Asia", "Regulatory compliance and registration support"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Atlanta, Georgia and Poland -> /about", "Product categories: blood collection, diagnostics, injection systems, PPE -> /about", "Markets served: AcuteCare, Long Term Care, Physician Offices, Blood Banks, Home Health, Animal Health -> /about", "Warehouse in Atlanta ships within 48 hours with free ground shipping -> /about", "Manufacturing base in US, Europe, Latin America, Asia -> /", "End-to-end capabilities: product design ideation, prototyping, clinical trials, re