UPDATE companies SET description='Mega Parts operates from Coon Valley, Wisconsin, where it maintains a 25,000-square-foot warehouse dedicated to parts for 1962–74 Mopar muscle cars.

Its catalog spans body panels, moldings, weatherstripping, fuel-system hardware, electrical harnesses, and interior trim, all organized through an online storefront. The 25,000-square-foot facility allows the company to keep thousands of part numbers on hand for immediate shipment.

Mega Parts primarily serves owners, restorers, and collectors of classic Mopar muscle cars, as well as restoration shops that need authentic or reproduction components for 1962–74 A-body, B-body, and E-body platforms. Customers range from individual enthusiasts rebuilding a single vehicle to professional shops sourcing hard-to-find items such as crossram components, convertible top hardware, or model-specific wiring harnesses.

The business distinguishes itself by focusing exclusively on the 1962–74 Mopar niche, offering both original NOS parts and reproduction items that are often unavailable elsewhere.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Molding Clip Sets", "Moldings Body Side", "Moldings Convertible Belt", "Moldings Deck Lid", "Moldings Door Top", "Moldings Drip Rail", "Moldings Quarter", "Moldings Rear Window", "Moldings Rocker Panel", "Moldings Tail Panel", "Moldings Valance", "Moldings Vinyl Top", "Moldings Wheel Opening", "Moldings Windshield", "A-Pillar Moldings", "Service Manuals CD", "Air Cleaner Service Instructions"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 25,000 square feet of warehouse space", "Specializes in 1962\u201374 Mopar muscle cars", "Carries new, used, NOS, NORS, and reproduction parts", "Extensive online catalog with thousands of part numbers"], "facts_used": ["Location: Coon Valley, Wisconsin -> db", "Warehouse size: 25,000 sq ft -> db", "Specialization: 1962-74 Mopar muscle cars -> db", "Product types: new, used, NOS, NORS, reproduction -> db", "Online store presence -> page:/", "Capability list (molding clips, moldings, manuals) -> db", "Product categories (body, electrical, fuel, trim) -> page:/", "Customer focus: Mopar owners, restorers, shops -> page:/"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We carry a large selection of new, used, NOS, NORS, and reproduction parts for your Mopar muscle car.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mega-parts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Meiden America Switchgear, Inc. (MAS) was founded in 2020 and is headquartered in Gray Court, South Carolina, near Greenville. The company operates as a subsidiary of Meidensha Corporation, a Japanese manufacturer founded in 1897 in Tokyo. MAS was established to serve the North American power grid with high-voltage vacuum circuit breakers (VCBs) and vacuum interrupters (VIs), drawing on its parent company’s 125-year history in the industry. President Yukihiro Takeshita leads the operation, which celebrated its grand opening and first shipment on February 9, 2021.

MAS designs, manufactures, tests, and sells 72.5 kV and 145 kV dry-air insulated dead-tank vacuum circuit breakers, as well as vacuum interrupter bottles. Meidensha pioneered vacuum interrupter technology in the mid-1960s and produced the world’s first 72.5 kV dry-air VCB in 2002, delivering more than 2,500 units globally, including over 1,000 to North American customers. The 145 kV dry-air VCB, introduced in late 2021, was another world first. The Gray Court facility handles full production from design through testing.

The company serves electric power utilities across North America that are seeking to replace sulfur hexafluoride (SF6) gas with environmentally friendly dry-air insulation. It also supplies vacuum interrupters to North American original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) for integration into their own switchgear. The database lists power and energy and automotive testing systems as served industries.

MAS positions its dry-air VCBs as a green alternative that eliminates SF6, a potent greenhouse gas, while offering zero emissions and low maintenance. The company’s mission is to lead the industry by providing high-value products that integrate cutting-edge technology and help customers meet environmental challenges.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Vacuum circuit breaker design and manufacturing", "Vacuum interrupter design and manufacturing", "High-voltage testing", "Field service engineering", "Dry-air insulated dead-tank VCB production"], "industries": ["Power and energy", "Automotive testing systems"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["World''s first 72.5 kV dry-air insulated dead-tank VCB (2002)", "World''s first 145 kV dry-air insulated dead-tank VCB (2021)", "Over 2,500 72.5 kV dry-air VCBs delivered worldwide", "Dry-air insulation eliminates SF6 greenhouse gas", "Vacuum interrupter technology pioneer since the 1960s"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Gray Court, South Carolina -> /about", "Founded in 2020 -> /about", "Subsidiary of Meidensha Corporation -> /about", "Design, manufacture, test and sell high-voltage vacuum circuit breakers and vacuum interrupters -> /about", "72.5 kV and 145 kV Dry Air VCBs -> /about", "More than 2,500 72.5kV Dry Air VCBs delivered worldwide -> /about", "World''s first 145 kV Dry Air VCB in late 2021 -> /about", "President Yukihiro Takeshita -> /about", "Grand Opening February 9, 2021 -> /about", "Industries: Power and energy, Automotive testing systems -> db", "Certification: ROHS -> db", "Website: https://www.meidenamericaswitchgear.com/ -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We design, manufacture, test and sell high-voltage vacuum circuit breakers (VCB) and vacuum interrupters (VI).", "founded_year": "2020", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance