UPDATE companies SET description='Melanzana Outdoor Clothing was founded in 1994 in Leadville, Colorado, as a local manufacturer of outdoor apparel. The company remains rooted in Leadville, where it began with a commitment to keep production domestic rather than outsourcing overseas. Ownership has transitioned to an employee-owned model, with more than 20 workers holding stock and a long-term goal of full employee ownership.

The company designs, cuts, and sews a range of outdoor garments—including hoodies, base layers, and accessories—at its Leadville factory and a newer facility in Alamosa. Together the two sites employ over 80 people in Leadville and 40 in Alamosa. Melanzana has developed more than 50 original product designs and emphasizes U.S.-made fabrics, though it sources Merino wool from Thailand when domestic equivalents are unavailable.

Melanzana sells directly to consumers through its Leadville retail store and online shop, serving outdoor enthusiasts and mountain communities. The brand has become a fixture in the outdoor industry, with its hoodie design language widely imitated. The company also supports local nonprofits through programs such as PB & Melly, which offers paid employee time for community work, and 1% For The Outdoors, a voluntary donation program funding conservation and recreation groups in the region.

Founded on the principle of local manufacturing, Melanzana differentiates itself through employee ownership, a focus on high-quality domestic textiles, and deep community investment. The company states that its evolution—from a single Leadville shop to a two-town operation—reflects a desire to maintain quality while reducing customer wait times.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cut and sew manufacturing", "Apparel design", "Fabric sourcing", "Retail operations"], "industries": ["Outdoor apparel", "Apparel manufacturing"], "materials": ["US-made fabrics", "Merino wool"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1994 in Leadville, CO -> /about", "Employee-owned with over 20 employee-owners -> /about", "Over 80 employees in Leadville, 40 in Alamosa -> /about", "Manufactures outdoor apparel (hoodies, base layers) -> /about", "Uses US-made fabrics, Merino wool from Thailand -> /about", "Over 50 original product designs -> /about", "Sells via Leadville retail store and online -> /about", "Community programs: PB & Melly, 1% For The Outdoors -> /about", "Headquarters: Leadville, Colorado -> db", "Website: melanzana.com -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a LOCAL manufacturer.", "founded_year": "1994", "employee_count": "Over 80 in Leadville, 40 in Alamosa", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='melanzana-outdoor-clothing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mercer Spring & Wire LLC operates from Townville, Pennsylvania. The company has been in the spring-manufacturing business for 70 years, building a depth of experience in cold-formed springs and wire forms. No founding year or founder names are publicly disclosed, and ownership structure has not been specified.

The shop specializes in cold-wound compression, torsion, and extension springs, as well as custom wire forms. It works with wire diameters from 0.008 inch to 0.500 inch in grades that include music wire, hard-drawn spring wire, oil-tempered spring wire, 302 and 316 stainless steel, beryllium copper, and both round and rectangular profiles. The facility is ISO 9001:2015 certified, and all products are made in the United States.

Customers come from automotive, electrical switch gear, safety equipment, air/gas/refrigeration, and medical equipment sectors. The company also lists miscellaneous industrial applications among its served markets.

