UPDATE companies SET description='Mercury Wire Products Inc. has operated from Spencer, Massachusetts since its founding in 1967. The company began as a custom wire and cable manufacturer and has remained independently owned, serving customers across the United States and internationally from its single Massachusetts facility.

The company designs and manufactures engineered wire, cable, and complete cable assemblies under one roof. Its capabilities span custom cable construction — selecting conductors, shielding, jacketing, and geometry for specific applications — through full assembly services that include crimping, connector termination, and testing. Production follows a value-stream model where a dedicated team owns each project from design through delivery, supported by lean manufacturing practices, in-house rapid prototyping, and Kanban-based inventory management.

Mercury Wire serves original equipment manufacturers in medical devices, aerospace, industrial equipment, and harsh-environment applications. Documented projects include waterproof push-rod inspection cables for sewer and pipeline inspection systems, plasma-cutting leads for cutting-technology OEMs, and cable assemblies for analytical instrumentation manufacturers. The company also supports power, signal, and specialty cable needs across industrial and medical systems.

Leadership emphasizes a people-first, continuous-improvement culture built around what it calls its True North principles. The stated differentiator is the value-stream ownership structure, which eliminates handoffs between engineering, production, and logistics to accelerate decisions and reduce lead times. The DIVE process — Discover, Design & Prototype, Build & Scale, Deliver & Support — formalizes this end-to-end accountability.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR Registered','REACH/RoHS Compliant','UL Approvals (Application-Specific)','CSA Approvals (Application-Specific)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable design and manufacturing", "Cable assembly and integration", "Custom engineering and prototyping", "Value-stream project ownership", "Lean manufacturing", "Kanban inventory management", "Rapid prototyping", "Design for manufacturability", "Crimping and termination", "Connector integration", "Cable testing and validation", "Waterproof cable construction", "High-flex cable design", "Shielded cable construction", "Multi-conductor cable manufacturing"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Aerospace", "Industrial equipment", "Plasma cutting technology", "Pipeline and sewer inspection", "Analytical instrumentation", "Power and signal distribution"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dedicated value-stream team owns each project from design through delivery", "Lean manufacturing with Kanban pull-based inventory management", "In-house rapid prototyping and custom engineering support", "ITAR registered with REACH/RoHS compliance and UL/CSA approvals", "Turnkey assembly including crimping, connector termination, and testing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1967 in Spencer, Massachusetts -> db, /", "Custom wire and cable manufacturer -> /", "Value-stream team model, lean manufacturing, Kanban inventory -> /", "Services: Custom Cable, Assembly, Custom Engineering and Prototyping -> /, /services", "Certifications: ITAR Registered, REACH/RoHS Compliant, UL & CSA Approvals -> /", "Industries: Medical, Aerospace, Plasma cutting, Sewer/pipeline inspection, Analytical instrumentation -> /", "DIVE Process (Discover, Design & Prototype, Build & Scale, Deliver & Support) -> /", "People-first, continuous-improvement culture, True North principles -> /about-us", "Turnkey assembly with crimping, connector termination, testing -> /services", "Waterproof push-rod inspection cable case study -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Mercury Wire is a custom cable manufacturer specializing in engineered wire, cable, and assembly solutions built for your specific application and environment.", "founded_year": "1967", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR Registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mercury-wire-products-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Meridian Cable, LLC, headquartered in St. Augustine, Florida, opened its first facility in 1994. The company operates a 7,000-square-foot plant in northeast Florida and owns a 30,000-square-foot production facility in Tanggu, China.

The company designs and manufactures custom cable assemblies, including RF, SMA, shielded, overmolded, and coil cord configurations. Its capabilities span cable design and engineering, custom extrusion (34 AWG to 12 AWG conductors), low-pressure insert molding using an LPMS Beta 300 machine, prototyping, 100% pre-production testing (continuity, integrity, polarity, functionality), qualification sampling, and volume manufacturing. An advanced life-testing lab validates designs under harsh conditions. Meridian maintains over 5,000 molds and tools, and designs more than 70 percent of the products it builds.

Customers rely on the firm for engineered solutions that cannot be sourced off the shelf, from concept through qualification to full-rate production.

Meridian differentiates itself by owning its Chinese facility, ensuring direct quality control and unchanged specifications from design to delivery. The company extrudes its own cable from raw copper, allowing specification adjustments, and provides U.S. warehousing with KanBan stocking programs. Every assembly undergoes 100% testing before shipment, and the team supports UL, MIL-SPEC, and CSA certification processes.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IATF 16949','UL-approved wire & cable extruder','UL certification for individual products','MIL-SPEC','CSA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable design & engineering", "Custom cable assembly manufacturing", "Wire harness assembly", "Coil cord manufacturing", "Overmolding / insert molding", "Custom cable extrusion", "Prototyping", "Pre-production testing (continuity, integrity, polarity, functionality)", "Qualification sampling", "Volume manufacturing", "Life/aging testing", "3D CAD design & modeling", "Low pressure molding (LPMS Beta 300)", "KanBan / stocking programs", "Distribution", "UL certification support", "MIL-SPEC compliance", "CSA certification support", "Shielded cable assembly", "RF cable assembly", "SMA connector assembly", "Medical cable assembly"], "industries": ["Military & defense", "Telecommunications", "Medical / healthcare", "Industrial control", "Broadcasting", "Retail security", "Automotive", "Aerospace", "Film"], "materials": ["Copper conductors (34 AWG to 12 AWG)", "Plastic resins for overmolding & extrusion"], "equipment": ["LPMS Beta 300 low pressure molding machine", "3D CAD design & modeling software", "Advanced life testing lab", "Automated testing systems", "Wire & cable extrusion equipment"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production (millions of units)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Designs over 70% of products in-house", "Owns and directly controls China manufacturing facility", "Extrudes custom cable from raw copper (34 AWG to 12 AWG)", "Maintains 